  {
   "title": "A haon, a dó: uimhreacha leo féin",
   "en": "Numbers on their own: labels and sums",
   "rule": "When a number stands on its own, as a label or in a sum, put a in front of it, with h before aon and ocht: seomra a dó, bus a haon, Bliain a hocht. In sums say is for plus, óna for minus (smaller number first), faoina for times and sin for equals.",
   "steps": [
    "Say the number in Irish: 8 is ocht.",
    "Put a in front, with h because ocht begins with a vowel: a hocht.",
    "Put it after the noun: Seomra a hocht."
   ],
   "example": {
    "prompt": "Seomra (8)",
    "answer": "Seomra a hocht."
   },
